# Copy this to `.env` (gitignored) for local development.
#
# muffin loads a .env from the directory you run it in, if one exists. Real
# environment variables always win, and production ships no .env — so this is a
# dev-only convenience with no effect on the VPS.
#
# THE MODEL KEY DOES NOT BELONG HERE ANY MORE (ADR-0039 amends ADR-0030).
# This file sits in the directory muffin runs from, which is the directory its
# own `fs_read` tool is scoped to — so one tainted turn (a web result in
# context, then "read .env") handed the key to the model. Put it here anyway and
# it still works, and the deny-list stops the agent reading it back; but the
# place it belongs is:
#
#   echo -n "$KEY" | muffin secret set provider_api_key --persist
#
# which writes $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/muffin/secrets/provider_api_key (0700/0600).
# That is still OUTSIDE ~/.muffin, so it survives
#   muffin uninstall --yes
# and the next `muffin init` finds it instead of prompting — the whole point of
# ADR-0030, minus the working-directory exposure.
#
#   sk-or-…  → OpenRouter (one key, every model)   https://openrouter.ai/keys
#   sk-ant-… → Anthropic direct                    https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
#
# `muffin doctor` tells you which store answered, so you can see the move landed.

# Optional: point dev at its own home so it never touches a real install.
# The VPS (prod) just leaves this unset and uses the default ~/.muffin.
# This is the kind of thing a .env is still for: not secret, per-checkout.
# MUFFIN_HOME=/Users/you/.muffin-dev
